---
import Section from "./Section.astro";

const layers = [
  {
    name: "Web app",
    kind: "React + TanStack Router",
    detail: "Shared rooms · conversation, activity, plan annotation, live preview · team auth",
  },
  {
    name: "Worker",
    kind: "Cloudflare Worker",
    detail: "Stateless router · Better Auth + Google OAuth · routes to Durable Object",
  },
  {
    name: "Durable Object",
    kind: "One per session",
    detail: "State machine · event log (SQLite) · WebSocket hub · multiplayer attribution · redaction",
  },
  {
    name: "Sandbox",
    kind: "Cloudflare Sandbox",
    detail: "Ephemeral Linux container · Pi SDK as library · cloned repo · live preview server",
  },
];
---
<Section id="architecture" eyebrow="Architecture" title="Four layers, one Cloudflare account">
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
    {layers.map((layer, i) => (
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <div class="grid gap-3 rounded-lg border border-line bg-surface p-5 sm:grid-cols-[180px_1fr] sm:items-center">
          <div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-fg">{layer.name}</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-fg-4">{layer.kind}</div>
          </div>
          <div class="text-sm text-fg-3">{layer.detail}</div>
        </div>
        {i < layers.length - 1 && (
          <div class="flex justify-center" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-4">↓ WebSocket</span>
          </div>
        )}
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p class="mt-6 font-mono text-xs text-fg-4">
    Pi SDK runs inside the sandbox as a library — not a CLI subprocess. Events stream
    sandbox → Durable Object → every connected web client in real time. A thin CLI client
    also exists for terminal-driven runs.
  </p>
</Section>
